# Python's cache folders and files, in every folder at any depth (lib, runs, and
# any folder added later). Python makes them by itself, so they never go into git.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# CHANGE (Nov 5): new files in tools/ are not added to git. tools/ holds test
# scripts that run on a computer, not on the hub. Files already in git, like
# tools/test_attachment_lifecycle.py, stay in git.
tools/
# CHANGE (Nov 9): the logs folder is never added to git with the code.
# tools/run_logged.py uploads new log files to the logs folder on GitHub by
# itself, without touching the code or any other files.
logs/
# CHANGE (Nov 10): __init__.py files are never added to git. The hub doesn't
# use them, and pybricksdev 2.3.1 and newer doesn't need them. On a computer
# with an older pybricksdev, uploading main.py fails with "Did you forget to
# put an __init__.py file". Fix that by updating it: pip install -U pybricksdev
__init__.py
